Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] llvm-libgcc: pass target flags when generating version script

gcc_s.ver.in detects ARM hard-float support from compiler predefined macros.
The custom preprocessing command only invokes CMAKE_C_COMPILER, unlike the
normal compile rules, so a cross compiler configured for ARMv7 hard-float is
invoked without its -mcpu and -mfloat-abi flags and fails the platform check.

Split CMAKE_C_FLAGS into a CMake list and pass it to the custom command so its
target view matches the objects and libraries whose symbols it describes.

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
 llvm-libgcc/CMakeLists.txt | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/llvm-libgcc/CMakeLists.txt b/llvm-libgcc/CMakeLists.txt
index 9e46ac98d6ee..dc779170529d 100644
--- a/llvm-libgcc/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/llvm-libgcc/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -100,8 +100,11 @@ set(LIBUNWIND_HAS_GCC_S_LIB OFF)
 add_subdirectory(${LLVM_LIBGCC_LIBUNWIND_PATH} ${LLVM_LIBGCC_LIBUNWIND_BINARY_DIR})
 
+separate_arguments(LLVM_LIBGCC_C_FLAGS NATIVE_COMMAND "${CMAKE_C_FLAGS}")
+
 add_custom_target(gcc_s.ver
   SOURCES ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/gcc_s.ver.in
   COMMAND ${CMAKE_C_COMPILER} -E
+    ${LLVM_LIBGCC_C_FLAGS}
     -xc ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/gcc_s.ver.in
     -o ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/gcc_s.ver
 )
